  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "PLAN.md Q1 — what happens when you point at a marked phrase",
  "explanation": "The fork is the click, not the hover: both routes light the same boxes, and only one of them hands you a verdict in a single gesture. Look at what hangs off the click — the arrows inside the option come along, and boxes already ruled on are left as they are, both rules the page already applies to a box-selection. The dead end off the hover is the cost of highlighting alone: you still box-select the option by hand, which is the work the group existed to remove. Leaves out the markup and the panel's own layout.",
